  "N26" [label="(30,3,0) Other nucleotides are coupled with irreversible terminators."];
  "N27" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-Conclusion: Matching nucleotides use reversible terminators and others use irreversible, so reversible/irreversible logic selects targets."];
  "N39" [label="(21,0,0) If selection stops after the second cycle with barcodes A and T, four subsets within the ATN barcode can be simultaneously selected."];
  "N39_B" [label="(31,0,0) Repeating cycles after deprotecting reversible terminators allows only oligos with target barcodes to be retrieved."];
  "N39_Final" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-Conclusion: Barcode-directed cycles support selection of oligo subsets and retrieval of oligos with target barcodes."];
  "N4" [label="(3,0,0) For effective PCR, each target subset must possess a unique selection region for primer pairs."];
  "N40" [label="(13,0,0) The method involves single-nucleotide resolution cyclic DNA synthesis and blocking of template oligos, and oligo subset selection was demonstrated with only a few nucleotides and without primer synthesis for each subset."];
