  "N44" [label="(18,1,0) The proposed method allows the selection of oligo subsets in a hierarchical manner."];
  "N45" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-Conclusion: Advancement enables hierarchy and method allows selection, so method supports hierarchy."];
  "N5" [label="(5,3,0) The synthesis burden increases in proportion to the number of oligonucleotide subsets."];
  "N6" [label="(8,2,0) Dedicating 40 nucleotides to the selection region is inefficient regardless of subset number."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This paper proposes a synthesis-and-selection method for targeted oligonucleotide subsets: short barcodes can encode 4^N subsets, single-nucleotide incorporations use reversible terminators for barcode-matching bases and irreversible terminators for other bases, the original oligo library is immobilized on solid substrates, target subsets are retrieved from the original template, and hierarchical selection avoids unique primer pairs for each subset.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
